  <title id="bdlensembledisagreement-title">Five independently trained networks agree on the data and disagree away from it</title>
  <desc id="bdlensembledisagreement-desc">Forty noisy samples of sin(x) lie in two shaded intervals, from -3 to -1 and from 1 to 3. Five tanh networks trained from different random initializations pass through the data almost identically. Between the intervals and beyond them their curves fan apart, and the band of plus or minus two predictive standard deviations around the ensemble mean widens, but not enough: from about x = 3.3 to 4.9, and below about x = -5, the dashed true function lies outside the band.</desc>
